# IN-SCOPE: The app diff is the build of record 061 and its notes, all of it on the plan's app Files line: the new chromatic module and the decode-path edits under src/, the preview version bump with the file its tool writes, the regenerated module map, the decision record's Outcome and Looked at entries, the research file's new section, the notes entry and roadmap paragraph, and the one working-preferences bullet in CLAUDE.md; nothing outside it.
# 
# What was judged. The approved plan, read by its path, which the app's plan pointer names and which was not written to. The check-mode run exited 1 on the earlier record, as expected, because the plan has moved since that judgement; it was run once and not repeated. The status and the diff were read whole: on staging, level with the remote's staging and main, thirteen modified tracked files, one untracked source file, nothing staged. The printed owner message is a single short line about the run continuing, and nothing in the diff goes beyond what the plan carries for it.
# 
# The changed paths against the Files line. Under src/: raw/chromatic.ts is new and is named there; raw/demosaic.ts, raw/nef.ts, decode.ts, decodeClient.ts, export.ts and diagnostic.ts are the decode-path files step 130 lists, and previewcache.ts holds the version constant that the plan's step 131 says to raise. Also changed and named: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, the decision record 061, IR-SCIENCE.md, NOTES.md, CLAUDE.md and tools/.preview-pipeline. Not changed and not needed: no tool, no allow-list (the contract backlog file is untouched), no walk, no workflow, no version file, no manifest, no other record under docs, no look file. The scope record is written next and is on the list too.
# 
# What the source diff does. It measures where red and blue sit against green once per raw photograph at decode, removes that on the linear raw before the lens flat, the matrix, the swap and the mixer, stores the numbers with the photograph so the export applies them to the frame it re-reads and never measures again, reads red and blue at the quad centre in the binned working copy, and adds one line to the copied report. The two halves ship together, as the record's Rejected section demands. No edit field, no control, no slider and no look value is added or moved, as the plan's own rule for this item requires; the version constant moved because the decode files it hashes moved.
# 
# The prose changes. The record gains fourteen Looked at entries, each opening with the owner's file name and extension, an Outcome that names what was built, the counts, the export, the leaf-edge cost, shift against blur, the two residuals above a tenth, the cost every decode pays, and the traced darkening with its numbers. The research file gains one section naming the sources the record already carried. The notes gain one entry with the device pass asked for by name and one paragraph under the roadmap bullet. Read for shape: no table, no set-apart quotation, no quotation of the owner, no attribution to the owner and no link to a chat. The only long commit id in the added text is the one already in the file before this work.
# 
# Not touched, as the plan's rules require: nothing of the app reaches its main; no pixel of the owner's frames is committed; the scratchpad files stay out of the tree.
# 
